<section class="section"><div class="section-gap case-v2"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="home-hero-content-wrap contact-v3"><div class="inner-hero-left blog-detail"><div class="project-badge"><div class="pill-dot"></div><div class="badge-text">AI &amp; Robotics</div></div><div class="hero-heading-wrap blog-detail"><h1 data-wf-target="[[[&quot;6ac5e94447485411ecc001bd&quot;,&quot;1234992f-0fc0-545b-c408-c8fdd3524429&quot;],[]]]">Building Intelligence Behind Autonomous </h1><p class="paragraph-regular contact-v2 blog-detail">ANANTACAST helped a robotics company design the AI architecture that lets its autonomous machines sense, decide, and respond in real time across complex environments.</p></div></div><div class="inner-hero-right blog-detail"><a data-wf--primary-button--variant="bg-white" data-wf-component-id="4c762986-7cae-1c12-bec9-1ecbb760ee61" data-wf-variant-state="21f200ea-2927-6f93-7fe0-867acd69adf4" href="/contact-v1" class="primary-button w-variant-21f200ea-2927-6f93-7fe0-867acd69adf4 w-inline-block"><div class="button-text-pill"><div class="button-text is-one">Start a Project</div><div class="button-text is-two">Start a Project</div></div><div class="button-arrow-pill"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" class="button-arrow"><path d="M15.8333 12.5002H9.99992H3.33325L3.33325 5.8335V5.3335" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M12.5 16.6668L16.6667 12.5002L12.5 8.3335" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" class="button-arrow"><path d="M15.8333 12.5002H9.99992H3.33325L3.33325 5.8335V5.3335" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M12.5 16.6668L16.6667 12.5002L12.5 8.3335" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div></div><div class="hero-image-wrap case-detail"><img src="/images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23.webp" loading="lazy" data-parallax="true" alt="Building Intelligence Behind Autonomous " sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 991px) 95vw, 939px" srcset="/images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23-p-500.webp 500w, /images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23-p-800.webp 800w, /images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23-p-1080.webp 1080w, /images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23-p-1600.webp 1600w, /images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23-p-2000.webp 2000w, /images/6ac5eabb8d118f7c2f7fb36f_d12a286cd27fac815b8c11e885e858296dfc8e23.webp 2400w" class="home-hero-image case-v2"/></div></div></div></section>

<section class="section black-800"><div class="section-gap blog"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="blog-body-wrap case-detail"><div class="case-detail-grid"><div data-to-top="0" class="case-detail-card"><div class="case-detail-label"><div class="pill-dot case-detail"></div><div class="badge-text case-detail">Client</div></div><div class="case-detail-value">Brightly</div></div><div data-to-top="2" class="case-detail-card"><div class="case-detail-label"><div class="pill-dot case-detail"></div><div class="badge-text case-detail">Industry</div></div><div class="case-detail-value">AI &amp; Robotics</div></div><div data-to-top="4" class="case-detail-card"><div class="case-detail-label"><div class="pill-dot case-detail"></div><div class="badge-text case-detail">Location</div></div><div class="case-detail-value">Boston, Massachusetts</div></div><div data-to-top="0" class="case-detail-card"><div class="case-detail-label"><div class="pill-dot case-detail"></div><div class="badge-text case-detail">Engagement</div></div><div class="case-detail-value">AI &amp; Intelligent Systems</div></div><div data-to-top="2" class="case-detail-card"><div class="case-detail-label"><div class="pill-dot case-detail"></div><div class="badge-text case-detail">Timeline</div></div><div class="case-detail-value">20 Weeks</div></div><div data-to-top="6" class="case-detail-card"><div class="case-detail-label"><div class="pill-dot case-detail"></div><div class="badge-text case-detail">Team</div></div><div class="case-detail-value">AI + Engineering</div></div></div><div class="blog-body-intro"><div data-to-top="0" class="section-badge"><div class="pill-dot"></div><div class="badge-text">THE PROJECT</div></div><p data-to-top="0" class="font-medium blog-body">Brightly builds autonomous machines for warehouses and outdoor sites. As its fleet grew, the onboard intelligence struggled to keep up, with slow responses, inconsistent behaviour, and a software stack that was becoming difficult to extend safely.</p><div data-to-top="0" class="project-details w-richtext"><p><strong>Services</strong></p><ul><li>AI Strategy</li><li>Machine Learning</li><li>Edge Computing</li><li>Systems Architecture</li></ul><h2>The Challenge</h2><p>The engineering team was talented and moving fast. What they needed was an architecture that could handle growing sensor data while keeping every machine safe, predictable, and responsive.</p><p>Perception, planning, and control had grown as separate systems over several years. Data moved between them through ad-hoc interfaces, adding delays that limited performance and made every new feature a risk to the stability of the whole fleet.</p><h3>The team needed clear answers to key questions:</h3><ol><li><strong>Where should decisions happen?</strong><br>Choosing between onboard and cloud processing affected speed and cost.</li><li><strong>How do we reduce response time?</strong><br>Machines needed to react faster to people and obstacles around them.</li><li><strong>How do models improve safely?</strong><br>New AI models had to be tested before reaching machines in the field.</li><li><strong>Can the stack support new products?</strong><br>The architecture had to serve future robot types, not just today's fleet.</li></ol><h2>The Approach</h2><p>ANANTACAST combined AI strategy, systems engineering, and rigorous testing to create an intelligence layer the team could build on with confidence for years to come.</p><h3>Discover</h3><p>We analyzed the full software stack, from sensor input to motor control, measuring where time was lost, which components were fragile, and how data and models flowed between machines and the cloud.</p><h3>Define</h3><p>We set clear performance and safety targets with the team, then ranked the improvements that would deliver the fastest gains in response time while keeping operational risk as low as possible.</p><h3>Architect</h3><p>We designed a modular edge AI architecture with clean interfaces between perception, planning, and control, plus a cloud pipeline for training, simulation, and safe over-the-air model updates.</p><h3>Validate</h3><p>Every change was proven in simulation and on a small test fleet before wider release, giving the team hard evidence on latency, reliability, and safety before deploying to customer sites.</p><h2>The Solution</h2><p>Rather than optimising individual algorithms, ANANTACAST rebuilt how intelligence flows through each machine and across the fleet. Faster onboard processing, clear system boundaries, and a safe update pipeline now allow the team to ship new capabilities without compromising reliability.</p><h3>An intelligence layer built for autonomy at scale.</h3><p>Machines now respond faster and more consistently, while a modular architecture lets the team add new sensors, models, and robot types without rebuilding the core system.</p><p><strong>Solution</strong></p><ul><li>Edge AI Architecture</li><li>Real-Time Perception Pipeline</li><li>Simulation & Testing Framework</li><li>Over-the-Air Model Updates</li></ul><blockquote>“ANANTACAST gave our machines a faster, more reliable brain and gave our engineers a platform they can keep building on with confidence.”</blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></section>

